From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: validol1979-ops <225744605+validol1979-ops@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:32:08 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] KV-head replication for n_kv < S (KVDesc rep): Qwen3 /
 Qwen3.5 / LFM2 at S > n_kv

When S % n_kv == 0 and n_q % S == 0, each slice takes n_q / S consecutive query heads and KV head
sid // rep, rep = S / n_kv; replicas compute their K/V redundantly (bit-identical caches).
compiler.KVDesc rep (owned_heads -> sid // rep), kernels/layouts.head_parallel_attention_weights (per-slice
q / k / v, K/V rows duplicated), attention G_loc, Spec.check relaxed in qwen3 / qwen35 / lfm2, images and
descriptors one KV head per slice when replicated; tiled / runtime paths. Existing layouts unchanged
(56 image / program / logit / DRAM comparisons = baseline). Tests: S = 4 / n_kv 2 and S = 2 / n_kv 1 tiny
Qwen3 / Qwen3.5 on the ISA (emulation, resident == per-position, byte-identical KV replicas);
test_config_matrix 39 passed (with patches 0005, 0006); Qwen3 / Qwen3.5 / kernels 176 passed, 14 skipped.
Enables Qwen3.5-2B (n_kv 2) at S = 4. Codex gpt-6-astra (high), reviewed.

